    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Race-realists often claim that specific IQ subtests like fluid reasoning or processing speed are the only \"pure\" measures of innate ability, arguing that cultural biases in verbal tests unfairly disadvantage Black individuals. They frequently point to evolutionary timelines suggesting that modern humans have been genetically isolated for thousands of years, using this to argue that distinct cognitive \"races\" evolved separately and that these traits are now fixed and unchangeable. They also often cite specific brain imaging studies claiming smaller brain volumes or different neural connectivity patterns in Black populations, interpreting these biological differences as direct evidence of lower cognitive capacity.\n\nHowever, these claims are fundamentally flawed because the studies they cite are often methodologically unsound, rely on biased samples, or ignore the overwhelming evidence that environmental factors like nutrition, stress, and education drive all observed cognitive differences. The idea that race is a valid biological category with fixed cognitive implications is a pseudoscientific construct with no basis in modern genetics, and relying on such logic to deconstruct arguments would require accepting false premises that have been thoroughly dismantled by the scientific community.",
